{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. ___. I’m Dr. ___. You’re here today for your third cycle of high-dose methotrexate for your CNS lymphoma. How have you been feeling since your last treatment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Morning, Doctor. I’ve been doing pretty well overall. No seizures, no headaches. Just this mild fullness in my right ear that hasn’t gone away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. The ear fullness isn’t new, right? And you haven’t had any fevers, nausea, or dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, nothing like that. It’s just pressure, like when you’re on a plane. But otherwise, I feel stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll keep an eye on it, but it doesn’t sound concerning. You’ve been taking the sodium bicarbonate at home as instructed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, started yesterday morning—every six hours like last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. That helps protect your kidneys during the methotrexate infusion. We’ll continue IV fluids with bicarbonate too. You’ll get the chemo infusion around noon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:08:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the leucovorin? I remember that helps reduce side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:09:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You’ll get leucovorin starting later today and continuing over the next couple of days to help clear the methotrexate safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my DDAVP for diabetes insipidus—I’ve been using it as usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:11:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep you on your regular DDAVP schedule. But we’ll monitor your sodium closely because IV fluids can dilute it. That’s been an issue in past cycles, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:12:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, last time my sodium dropped. I was a bit confused for a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll check your sodium twice daily and adjust if needed. If it starts to drop, we may hold one dose of DDAVP, like we did before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:15:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. And my blood pressure and seizure meds are the same?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-09-26 10:16:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll stay on lisinopril and levetiracetam. No changes there. And we’ll keep your clonazepam and trazodone for anxiety and sleep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-09-26 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. The methotrexate infusion just started. It’ll run over the next few hours. How are you feeling so far?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-09-26 12:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No issues. Just a little nervous, but otherwise fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-09-26 12:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely normal. We’ll keep monitoring you. Let us know if you feel nausea, dizziness, or anything unusual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-09-26 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Infusion is complete. You did great—no immediate side effects. We’ll start your leucovorin soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-09-26 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. When will you know if the drug is clearing okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-09-26 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll check your methotrexate level tomorrow morning. It should be down from the peak. We keep checking until it’s below 0.1, then we’re safe to discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-09-26 14:35:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my sodium? Any change?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-09-26 14:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was 136 on admission—normal. We’ll check again tonight and tomorrow. We’re watching closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-09-27 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are back. Sodium is 130—slightly low. We’re going to hold your morning DDAVP dose to see if it stabilizes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-09-27 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe? I don’t want my DI to flare up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-09-27 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s just one dose. We’re giving you IV fluids, which can lower sodium, so holding DDAVP briefly helps balance it. We’ll restart it tomorrow if your sodium holds steady."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-09-27 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust you. Any other lab changes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-09-27 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your methotrexate level is down to 0.11—excellent. That means it’s clearing well. One more level tomorrow, and if it’s below 0.05, we can plan for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-09-27 07:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news. And my blood pressure? Still okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-09-27 07:27:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 128 over 74 this morning—perfect. You’ve stayed well-controlled on lisinopril."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-09-27 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re continuing your leucovorin and IV fluids. You’re doing well overall."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-09-27 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m feeling tired, but no nausea or pain. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-09-27 10:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, fatigue is common. Your body is processing the chemo. Rest as much as you need."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-09-28 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your methotrexate level is now 0.04. That’s low enough for safe discharge. Your sodium is stable at 131."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-09-28 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great! So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-09-28 07:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’ll send you home on your regular DDAVP. But please get your sodium checked in a few days to make sure it stays stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-09-28 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Any other lab work?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-09-28 07:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, a full electrolyte panel—sodium, potassium, creatinine. Fax the results to Dr. ___’s office."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-09-28 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my dexamethasone? Still the same dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-09-28 07:10:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re tapering it down to 2 mg daily, as planned. That’s one tablet by mouth each day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-09-28 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can manage that. And the sodium bicarbonate?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-09-28 07:13:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue one tablet every six hours starting 24 hours before your next admission. Same as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2184-09-28 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you for walking me through everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2184-09-28 07:16:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You tolerated this cycle very well. No complications, and your labs look good. We’ll see you in follow-up with neuro-oncology."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2184-09-28 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that. I’ll make sure to get those labs done and call if anything feels off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2184-09-28 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Call us if you have nausea, confusion, or excessive urination. Otherwise, rest and take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2184-09-28 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in before discharge. All set for home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2184-09-28 15:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve got my meds and instructions. Ready to go."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2184-09-28 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great this admission. We’ll keep monitoring your progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2184-09-28 15:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I’ll follow up as instructed."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-09-26 09:56:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-09-28 21:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 65-year-old man with a history of CNS lymphoma, diabetes insipidus, and histiocytosis X was admitted for his third cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. He presented in stable condition, reporting mild right ear fullness but no other symptoms. He tolerated the methotrexate infusion well without acute side effects. IV fluids with sodium bicarbonate were administered to support methotrexate clearance, and leucovorin rescue was continued. Methotrexate levels decreased appropriately, reaching 0.04 by discharge. Hyponatremia developed during treatment, with serum sodium dropping to 130, prompting a one-time hold of DDAVP; sodium stabilized at 131. Dexamethasone was tapered to 2 mg daily per protocol. The patient remained seizure-free on levetiracetam and normotensive on lisinopril. He was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to monitor electrolytes and continue home medications.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Other malignant lymphomas, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Diabetes insipidus",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Hip joint replacement",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, without mention of intractable epilepsy",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Sleep disturbance, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
